CAT = "sfadminConfig"; SEG = "CFG"
Q = [
("A company wants sales reps to see only the opportunities they own, while managers see their team's deals. What should the admin set first?",
 'A Private org-wide default', ['A Public Read Only default', 'A criteria-based sharing rule', 'A permission set group'],
 'Org-wide defaults set the most restrictive baseline access. With Opportunity set to Private, the role hierarchy then lets managers see records owned by the people below them.'),
("A manager in the role hierarchy can see a subordinate's private accounts. Which feature gives the manager that access?",
 'The role hierarchy', ["The manager's profile", 'Manual sharing', 'An account team'],
 'Access rolls up the role hierarchy: users in higher roles get the same access as the owners of records below them, as long as Grant Access Using Hierarchies is on.'),
('For which objects can an admin turn off Grant Access Using Hierarchies?',
 'Custom objects only', ['Standard objects only', 'Any object in the org', 'No objects at all'],
 "The setting is always on for standard objects. Only custom objects let the admin clear it so managers do not inherit access to their subordinates' records."),
('A user needs one extra object permission that no one else on her profile should get. What is the best way to grant it?',
 'Assign a permission set', ['Clone and edit her profile', 'Create a new role', 'Add a sharing rule'],
 'Permission sets add permissions to individual users without changing their profile, so one user can get extra access while the rest of the profile stays the same.'),
('How many profiles can be assigned to a single user?',
 'Exactly one', ['Up to two', 'As many as needed', 'One per app'],
 'Every user has exactly one profile. Extra permissions come from permission sets and permission set groups, which a user can have many of.'),
('An admin bundles five permission sets into a permission set group but must remove one permission for this group only. What should be used?',
 'A muting permission set', ['A second profile for the group', 'A criteria-based sharing rule', 'A restriction rule on the object'],
 "A muting permission set inside a permission set group turns off chosen permissions for the group's users without editing the permission sets it contains."),
('Users can read the Account object but must not see the Annual Revenue field. Which setting hides it?',
 'Field-level security', ['Org-wide defaults', 'Account sharing rules', 'Role hierarchy'],
 'Field-level security, set in profiles and permission sets, controls whether a user can see or edit each field. Sharing settings control which records, not which fields.'),
('Which statement about sharing rules is true?',
 'They can only open up access', ['They can lower the org default', 'They replace the role hierarchy', 'They apply to one user only'],
 'Sharing rules extend access beyond the org-wide default to groups of users. They can never be used to restrict access below the baseline.'),
('The admin wants accounts in the West region, whatever their owner, shared with a West Sales public group. Which sharing rule type fits?',
 'Criteria-based sharing rule', ['Owner-based sharing rule', 'Manual sharing by each owner', 'Apex managed sharing code'],
 'A criteria-based sharing rule shares records whose field values meet the criteria, such as Region equals West. Owner-based rules share by who owns the record.'),
('A rep uses the Sharing button to share one account with a colleague. What happens to that share when the account owner changes?',
 'The manual share is removed', ['It transfers to the new owner', 'It turns into a sharing rule', 'It stays until someone deletes it'],
 'Manual shares are tied to the current owner. When ownership changes, manual sharing created by the old owner is removed.'),
('A user leaves the company today but owns records used in an active flow, so the admin cannot deactivate the account yet. What should the admin do?',
 'Freeze the user', ['Delete the user', 'Reset the password', "Change the user's role"],
 'Freezing stops the user from logging in at once while the admin reassigns records or removes dependencies. Users can never be deleted, only deactivated.'),
('What happens to a user license when a user is deactivated?',
 'It becomes available', ['It is deleted from the org', 'It stays assigned', 'It moves to a manager'],
 "Deactivating a user frees the license for someone else, while the user's records and history stay in the org."),
('A profile has login IP ranges set. What happens when a user on that profile tries to log in from outside those ranges?',
 'The login is refused', ['They get a verification code', 'They log in as read only', 'Their manager is emailed'],
 'Login IP ranges on a profile block logins from any address outside the ranges. Trusted IP ranges for the org only skip identity verification; they do not block.'),
('Support agents must not log in on weekends. Where does the admin restrict this?',
 'Login hours on the profile', ['Business hours in Company Settings', 'Session timeout settings', "The agents' role in the hierarchy"],
 'Login hours are set on the profile. Outside them users cannot log in, and anyone already logged in is logged out when the hours end.'),
('A regional manager should reset passwords and edit users in his own region, without being a full admin. Which feature allows this?',
 'Delegated administration', ['A muting permission set', 'The Login As feature', 'A public group with admin rights'],
 'Delegated administration lets chosen users manage users in specified roles and their subordinates, and assign specified profiles and permission sets.'),
("Which tool scores an org's security settings against Salesforce's recommended baseline?",
 'Health Check', ['Setup Audit Trail', 'Optimizer report', 'Field history tracking'],
 'Health Check compares password, session and network settings with a baseline and lists the risky ones so the admin can fix them.'),
("The security team asks who changed a profile's permissions last month. Where does the admin look?",
 'Setup Audit Trail', ['Login History', 'Field history tracking', 'Debug logs'],
 'Setup Audit Trail records changes made in Setup, such as profile and permission edits, along with who made them and when.'),
('Which org-wide default does Salesforce set for the detail object in a master-detail relationship?',
 'Controlled by Parent', ['Private', 'Public Read/Write', 'Public Read Only'],
 "Access to a detail record follows access to its master record, so the detail object's org-wide default is Controlled by Parent and cannot be set separately."),
('A user can see an opportunity on an account she cannot otherwise access. What gives her read access to that parent account?',
 'Implicit sharing', ['A manual share', "Her profile's View All", 'The account team'],
 'Implicit sharing grants read access to a parent account when a user has access to its child opportunities, cases or contacts.'),
('Which object permission lets a user see every record of that object regardless of sharing?',
 'View All', ['Read', 'View All Records in the role', 'Edit'],
 'View All on an object overrides sharing for that object. Read only lets the user read the records sharing already gives them.'),
('An admin needs to troubleshoot what a user sees, but Login As is not offered for that user. What usually has to happen first?',
 'The user grants login access', ['The user is frozen for an hour', "The admin's role is raised above them", 'A sandbox is refreshed from production'],
 'Unless the org lets administrators log in as any user, the user must first grant login access from their settings for a set period.'),
('A company changed its fiscal year to start in April and needs quarters named its own way. What should the admin know before enabling custom fiscal years?',
 'It cannot be turned off', ['It deletes past forecasts', 'It applies to one profile', 'It needs a new org'],
 'Once custom fiscal years are enabled they cannot be disabled, and they affect forecasting, reports and quotas, so plan carefully first.'),
('What is true once multiple currencies are enabled in an org?',
 'They cannot be disabled', ['Users must share one currency', 'Reports show only one code', 'Opportunities lose amounts'],
 'Enabling multiple currencies is permanent. Each user has a personal currency, and amounts convert using the rates the admin maintains.'),
('Opportunity amounts should convert at the exchange rate in effect on the close date. Which feature does this?',
 'Advanced currency management', ['A change to the corporate currency', 'A formula field on Opportunity', 'A validation rule on Close Date'],
 'Advanced currency management adds dated exchange rates, so opportunities and their products convert using the rate for the close date.'),
('Case escalation should count only the hours the support team works. What does the admin define?',
 'Business hours', ['Login hours', 'Holidays in the role', 'Session timeout'],
 'Business hours (with holidays) tell escalation rules, entitlements and milestones which hours count. Login hours only limit when users can log in.'),
('Which statement about My Domain is correct?',
 'Every org must have one', ['It is only for portals', 'It changes the org ID', 'It turns off single sign-on'],
 'My Domain gives the org its own login URL and is required for features such as Lightning components and single sign-on; all orgs now have one.'),
('A records clerk only uses one custom app. How can the admin make sure she sees just that app?',
 'Assign the app to her profile', ['Delete the other apps from the org', 'Hide the other tabs with sharing', 'Move her to a lower role'],
 "Lightning apps are made visible by profile (and by permission set). Giving the clerk's profile access to that one app limits what the App Launcher shows her."),
('A sales group needs Edit access on opportunities owned by members of the Partner team role and its subordinates. What is the simplest way?',
 'An owner-based sharing rule', ['Manual sharing on each opportunity', 'A higher org-wide default for all', 'A new profile for the group'],
 'An owner-based sharing rule shares records owned by a role, role and subordinates, or group with another group, at Read Only or Read/Write.'),
('The admin wants developers to test a release with a full copy of production data and metadata. Which sandbox type fits?',
 'Full sandbox', ['Developer sandbox', 'Developer Pro sandbox', 'Scratch org'],
 'A Full sandbox copies all production data and metadata. Developer and Developer Pro copy metadata only, and Partial Copy takes a sample of data from a template.'),
('Users on one profile must change passwords more often than the rest of the org. Where can the admin set this?',
 'Password policies on the profile', ['Session settings for the whole org', 'The role hierarchy', 'A permission set group with expiry'],
 'A profile can carry its own password policies, which override the org-wide password policies for users on that profile.'),
]
